{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1374214-what-kind-of-dm-st-sg-you-are","id":1374214,"title":"What kind of DM/ST/SG you are?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-11T13:29:21-07:00","id":1374214,"title":"What kind of DM/ST/SG you are?","content":"What combination of D&amp;D classes points to your game running style? For me, it's probably Artificer/Cleric/Wizard combo.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent.fiev1-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/89784924_10213854856080456_4239186257919344640_n.jpg?_nc_cat=107&amp;_nc_sid=e007fa&amp;_nc_eui2=AeF9CvPiz7p-ugBZ-emRwMkWWioKCkhO-OW8xAU8AYZf7PzEa-vpe6foahsmKOEVjMlQ68mVhqQhbvPFG67RNhxMbH88LNwP6lvEH-DfpfBxDg&amp;_nc_ohc=U2qJ1a21A4gAX9ahynq&amp;_nc_ht=scontent.fiev1-1.fna&amp;oh=c316e92322b6415415268ea22d7aa5b8&amp;oe=5E93AA18\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:48:47-07:00","id":1374223,"title":"","content":"My goal is to be all of the above, but if I can only pick one, probably bard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T13:58:55-07:00","id":1374224,"title":"","content":"For me id say its even between Ranger and Sorcerer.<br /> But id love to be a better Wizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:15:42-07:00","id":1374228,"title":"","content":"Kind of a mix of Warlock and Wizard I guess. I mainly aim for a good, memorable storyline with lots of world building and tend to build the story heavily around player backstory hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T14:50:39-07:00","id":1374232,"title":"","content":"I'm probably a sorcerer with the problem being that I approach things from the wizard route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T15:05:40-07:00","id":1374234,"title":"","content":"I've had few enough chances to DM that I can't fully say I've figured out my style. But the way I've come to approach the game in my limited experience is a mix of Wizard and Ranger. I like to plan ahead, because having material on hand makes it easier in the moment. And I favor a sandbox style, where I plop the PCs down in a game world and let them find the adventure. I want to grant my players the freedom to choose their own path, but I also like to curate encounters.<br /> <br /> If there's one way I'm deficient as a Wizard, it's that while I do A LOT of lore building (I have literal months between games), I'm not the best at thinking up puzzles. It's an area of the game I'd love to work on, as I think making puzzles could serve to engage the players in ways other than fighting or making ability checks.<br /> <br /> A bit of the Cleric applies as well, in the sense that I've just memorized a lot of rules. (Though never as well as I'd like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-11-2020, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T15:07:12-07:00","id":1374235,"title":"","content":"Would be nice to be them all, in ST'ing I lean between Warlock/Rogue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T16:24:54-07:00","id":1374251,"title":"","content":"I used to be very Wizard/Warlock. These days I'm trying to dabble in a bit more of everything and get more comfortable with my Sorcerer/Paladin side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T19:48:29-07:00","id":1374280,"title":"","content":"No mindflayer? I'm disappointed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T21:10:14-07:00","id":1374290,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a>, maybe I need to change my Wizard answer for Ranger, too? I like to build setting - or mini-setting - and give players main plot idea and let them loose with it. It's a problem, sometimes, like I have right now in my games:<br /> <br /> ( <b>CoD</b>, 800 AD ) Viking werewolfs are going from Uppsala in Sweden to Constantinopole in Byzantium. For months ( years even ) I build <i>Queen of Cities</i> setting - as literal <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137216-dark-eras-fan-byzantine-empire?p=1352050#post1352050\">fan Dark Era about Byzantine Empire</a> - and lead my players there. Only they do not follow it. They stick in previous, backward 'last stop' location, checking leads about mysterious sickness in normal mortal characters that cannot possibly know anything about it. But they do it still. It's like 6th game session on things that should only take maybe two, at most. On the other hand, I ended the ways to make it more dire - and maybe I over do it, as players are thinking they cannot travel to Constantinopole to let live their co-player character, as he will not enough time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's like the need of the plot - or rather 'deadlines' - are fighting with me over the idea to let players just play with setting. But they are playing wrong setting now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-12-2020, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T21:58:15-07:00","id":1374297,"title":"","content":"On the subject, satirical take on the subject...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><a href=\"https://thehardtimes.net/harddrive/dungeon-master-finally-writes-perfect-campaign-distributes-scripts-to-players/\" target=\"_blank\">Dungeon Master Finally Writes Perfect Campaign, Distributes Scripts to Players</a></b></span><br /> <br /> COLORADO SPRINGS, Colo. \u2014 Dungeon Master Daniel Hyde recently finished writing his ideal D&amp;D campaign and released the final draft of its script to his players, according to sources familiar with the situation. \u201cI\u2019ve done it,\u201d said Hyde. \u201cI\u2019ve authored the greatest campaign imaginable, and as long as everyone memorizes their characters\u2019 lines before our next game, absolutely nothing can go wrong.\u201d<br /> While most members of the party lauded the plot, characters, and overall writing therein, they were also baffled and frustrated by the lack of room left for the players to impact the story. Members of Hyde\u2019s Sunday tabletop group reflected these sentiments.<br /> \u201cIt definitely caught us all off guard,\u201d said Allison Wilcox, one of Hyde\u2019s regular players. \u201cWe all love D&amp;D because we get to roleplay, solve puzzles and participate in an interactive story. The script Dan sent us doesn\u2019t leave room for any of that. It includes the predetermined results of our rolls and even what we\u2019re supposed to say out of character and when we can go to the bathroom and stuff. I\u2019ve had DMs railroad games before, but this is next-level.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T23:57:20-07:00","id":1374717,"title":"","content":"Sorcerer/Warlock. Minimal prep, maximum emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T05:12:51-07:00","id":1374742,"title":"","content":"I'd be curious what people would guess me to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T08:17:55-07:00","id":1374762,"title":"","content":"Hmm tricky...<br /> If I can only pick one I'm a warlock, your past is never safe from me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T11:12:07-07:00","id":1374776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1374214-what-kind-of-dm-st-sg-you-are?p=1374742#post1374742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be curious what people would guess me to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my very limited experience with you as an ST, a Warlock. But, I could also see you as a Cleric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}